 T(r"""Let $\mathcal{X}\subset\mathbb{R}^p$ be a compact nonempty set of inputs and $f:\mathbb{R}^p\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^n$ be a continuous function. In this work, we tackle the general problem of reachability analysis, i.e., characterizing the set of reachable outputs $y=f(x)$ for all possible inputs $x\in\mathcal{X}$. This problem is also often referred to as uncertainty propagation. Mathematically, the objective consists of efficiently computing an accurate approximation of the reachable set $\mathcal{Y}\subset\mathbb{R}^n$, which is defined as""", [90, 161, 523, 226]),
